.TH MOIN-MKWIKI 8 "October 2026" "MoinMoin 1.11.0+md1" "MoinMoin"
.SH NAME
moin\-mkwiki \- create a new MoinMoin wiki instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moin\-mkwiki
[\fB\-n\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fILANG\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fISUPERUSER\fR]
[\fB\-u\fR \fIUSER\fR] [\fB\-g\fR \fIGROUP\fR] \fIDIRECTORY\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B moin\-mkwiki
copies the wiki templates of /usr/share/moin into the new directory
\fIDIRECTORY\fR: the wiki data (data/, underlay/), a wikiconfig.py with a
random secret, and the server scripts moin.wsgi, moin.cgi, moin.fcgi,
moin.scgi and wikiserverconfig.py, adapted to the instance directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-n " NAME"
name of the wiki (default: the directory name)
.TP
.BI \-l " LANG"
default language (default: en)
.TP
.BI \-s " SUPERUSER"
name of the superuser, who also gets all ACL rights (acl_rights_before);
the account is created later with \fBmoin account create\fR
.TP
.BI \-u " USER" ", \-g " GROUP
owner of the files when run as root (default: www\-data)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR moin (1),
/usr/share/doc/python3\-moinmoin\-markdown/README.Debian
